==Trivia==
*Cat Base Mini was given his [[True Form]] in the same update as the Reinforcements, [[Version 9.9 Update|9.9]], despite being part of a separate group.
*The Reinforcements' Evolved Forms were the first units to have single-slot [[Cat Combo|Combos]]. Prof. Cat Jobs has [[Good Jobs! (Combo)|Good Jobs!]], Rich Cat Sr. has [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Ritches]] and Sniper the Heavy has [[Thirteen (Combo)|Thirteen]].
*Each Reinforcement's Evolved Form is based on a different anime or manga character:
**Prof. Cat Jobs is a reference to [[wikia:astroboy:Hiroshi Ochanomizu|Hiroshi Ochanomizu]] from ''Astro Boy''. His Japanese name is Dr. Okamenomizu, and he shares the same curly white hair and four-buttoned suit as Ochanomizu.
**Rich Cat Sr. is a reference to Bakabon's Papa from ''Tensai Bakabon''. In addition to wearing the same headband and bellyband that Bakabon's Papa is known for, his Japanese name is Nekobon's Papa, and his Japanese description states that he is an unemployed father who is a living example of what not to do.
***Rich Cat Sr.'s knockback sprite resembles [[wikia:osomatsukun:Media:Tumblr nyuxjihUWx1v0jxj1o4 250.png|Iyami's "sheeh!" pose]] from ''Osomatsu-kun'', making him the only Reinforcement to reference more than one character.
**Sniper the Heavy is a reference to Golgo 13 from the manga of the same name. His Japanese name is Negolgo, he is described as "a grim assassin who never fails a contract," and his Cat Combo is named Thirteen.
*Prior to [[Version 11.2 Update|version 11.2]], [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]], [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Piledriver Cat]], [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter Cat]], [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]] and [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]] were part of their own set called Grandon Mining Corps.
*As of [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]], both the Reinforcements and Limited Edition units are permanently part of most [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] sets.